## 00887 PATIENT=1 DOCTOR=2 FAMILY_MEMBER=3
3: Doctor, he fell off his bike outside the house, and cut his lip, and one of his front teeth is loose. ~ cc s1 s2
2: Thank you. Is that right, Dev? You came off your bike? ~
1: Yeah. I hit the kerb. ~
2: When did it happen? ~ s1
3: About an hour ago. I brought him straight here. ~ s1
2: Did you hit your head, Dev, or black out at all? ~ n1
1: No. I put my hands out and my mouth hit the ground. ~ n1
3: He was awake the whole time, he was crying straight away. ~ n1
2: Good. Any neck pain, or pain anywhere else? ~ s3
1: My wrist hurts a bit. The left one. ~ s3
2: Any vomiting or dizziness since? ~ r1
1: No, nothing like that. I feel okay, just my mouth hurts. ~ r1
2: Has he taken anything for the pain? ~ m1
3: I gave him a spoonful of that pink medicine for children, I don't know the name. ~ m1 u1
2: Do you know how much? ~ m1
3: Just a teaspoon, I think. ~ m1 u1
2: Thank you. Does he have any medical conditions? ~ h1
3: Asthma, mild. Nothing else. ~ h1
2: Let me check his pulse, oxygen and temperature. ~
1: Okay. ~ pause=10
2: Pulse 96, oxygen 99 percent, temperature 36.8. ~ v
3: Is it all right? ~
2: All normal. Dev, can you open your mouth wide for me? ~
1: Ahh. ~ pause=14
2: There's a cut on the inside of the upper lip, about a centimetre long, and it's stopped bleeding. ~ x1
3: What about the tooth? ~
2: The upper left front tooth is loose, and slightly pushed back. It looks like a baby tooth, so we need to be careful. ~ x2 d1
1: Will it fall out? ~
2: Possibly. I'd like you to see a dentist today, and they may want an X-ray of the tooth. ~ p1 p2
3: I'll take him straight there. ~
2: The cut doesn't need stitches. Rinse with salt water, and give soft foods for a few days. ~ c1
1: Okay. ~
2: And his wrist is tender but he can move it. If the pain gets worse, or it swells, we should X-ray it. ~ x3 p3
3: We'll watch it. ~
2: If he vomits, becomes sleepy, or the bleeding starts again, come back to us immediately. ~ f1
3: Thank you, doctor. ~
